# {{lb|en|slang|now|_|historical}} An unskillful, awkward person. {{defdate|from the later part of the 19th c}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:P. G. Wodehouse|title=w:There's Always Golf|location=London|publisher=w:The Strand Magazine|year=1936|url=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=BKHk3hKEKY8C&lpg=PA361&ots=QLuxvbOmbn&dq=wodehouse%20in%20whom%20I%20recognized%20a%20prominent%20local%20dub&pg=PA361#v=onepage&q=wodehouse%20in%20whom%20I%20recognized%20a%20prominent%20local%20dub&f=false|passage=As I came over the hill, I saw Ernest Plinlimmon and his partner, in whom I recognized a prominent local '''dub''', emerging from the rough on the right. Apparently, the latter had sliced from the tee, and Ernest had been helping him find his ball.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1969|author=Robert L. Vann|title=The Competitor|volume=2-3|page=135
|passage=The miser, a-seeking lost gelt, / The doughboy, awaiting the battle, / May possibly know how I felt / While the long years dragged by as the dealer / As slow as the slowest of '''dubs''', / Stuck out the last helping of tickets / 'Till I lifted—the Bullet of Clubs!}}

